{
  "note": "The mockup against the native SwiftUI port, every screen: the mockup is the design and the port follows it. Remaining differences are the mockup's demo data the native demo doesn't carry (deck B's +1 key shift, CUE markers, 71% master), and glyph edges. 'aa' forgives glyph-edge anti-aliasing. 'budget' is a ratchet: lower it whenever a change brings the count down and never raise it to pass. home-overlays hides the synthetic demo waveforms on both sides so everything drawn over them is held to a tight budget; the demo strokes rasterise differently in Chromium and only count in home. home-tall checks the elastic height at its 4:3 limit.",
  "out": "out/native-diff",
